e>Kim</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Chung</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Koh</surname><given-names>JY</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoon</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Jo</surname><given-names>AY</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>MY</given-names></name><name><surname>Koh</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hwang</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Suh-Kim</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>YS</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>KS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Differential actions of the proneural genes encoding Mash1 and neurogenins in Nurr1-induced dopamine neuron differentiation</article-title><source>J Cell Sci</source><year>2006</year><volume>119</volume><fpage>2310</fpage><lpage>2320</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16723737</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bertrand</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Castro</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Guillemot</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Proneural genes and the specification of neural cell types</article-title><source>Nat Rev Neurosci</source><year>2002</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>517</fpage><lpage>530</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12094208</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kageyama</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohtsuka</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hatakeyama</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohsawa</surname><given-names>R</giv